<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBHYP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Orthopyroxene-gabbro, hypersthene"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBIB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro, biotite-bearing"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Leucogabbro"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro, migmatitic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBMG> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro and microgranite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBMGBR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock and microgabbroic-rock"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBMS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock and metasedimentary rock"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBNO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbronorite - A type of gabbro. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is a gabbro with plagioclase 10 - 90%, pyroxene 5 - 90% (>5% clino- and orthopyroxene) and olivine <5% of plagioclase + pyroxene + olivine. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 13, 14."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBNR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro and norite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock - A type of coarse-grained normal crystalline rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, this class includes gabbro, monzogabbro, and similar rocks. The term may be used as a field classification when an accurate mineral mode from thin section examination is not available. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 9, 10."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBRA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock, appinitic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBRCNT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock, contaminated"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBRH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock, hornfelsed"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBRMG> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbroic-rock, magnetic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro (s.s.) - A type of gabbro. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is a gabbro with plagioclase 10 - 90%, pyroxene 5 - 90% (<5% orthopyroxene) and olivine < 5% of plagioclase + pyroxene + olivine. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 13, 14."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBSH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro, sheared"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBUM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro and ultramafic rock"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GBXEN> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro, xenolithic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GCSP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granofels, calcsilicate-rock and granofelsic semipelite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GCSQ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granofels, calcsilicate-rock and quartzite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite - A type of granitic-rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is a coarse-grained crystalline igneous rock whose mineral mode plots in field 4 of the quartz - alkali feldspar - plagioclase - feldspathoid (QAPF) diagram. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1 and figs. 9, 11, 12."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDAD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite and appinitic diorite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDBI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, biotite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDDI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite and diorite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDDL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, diorite and leucogranite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDFO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, foliated"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDGNS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, gneissose"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDHB> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, hornblende"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDHP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, k-feldspar-megacrystic-hornblende"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GDHY> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite, hyperstene"@en .
