<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GHMG> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Hornblende granodiorite and monzogranite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GHSCH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Schist, garnet-hornblende"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GLBA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Glassy basalt and glassy andesite"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GLCL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, glauconitic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GLIG> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Glassy-igneous-rock - A type of fine-grained normal crystalline rock. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GLMDST> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mudstone, glauconitic"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GLSCH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Schist, glaucophane"@en .
