<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MAFI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mafite - A type of fine-grained normal crystalline rock. It is a general term used for dark-coloured aphanitic rocks. In the Rock Classification Scheme, the class includes andesitic-rock, basaltic-rock, phonolitic-rock, tephritic-rock and foiditic-rock. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.2 and fig. 17."@en .
