<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MCANOR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Micro-anorthositic-rock - A type of medium-grained normal crystalline rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is the medium-grained equivalent of anorthositic-rock. The class includes micro-anorthosite and similar rocks. The term may be used as a field classification when an accurate mineral mode from thin section examination is not available. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1."@en .
