<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MEIM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Meimechite - A type of picritic-rock. Its definition is as shown in British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.2 and figs. 17b, 22."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Metalimestone and dolostone"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melilitite - A type of ultramafic-melilitic-rock. Melilitite is the general name for fine-grained melilitic rocks, and they are classified according to their melilite - olivine - clinopyroxene content. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 6.2 and fig. 28b."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELKLO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melilitite, kalsilite-leucite-olivine - A type of melilitite. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, figs. 29, 30. Synonym: katungite."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELKP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melilitite, kalsilite-phlogopite - A type of melilitite. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, figs. 29, 30. Synonym: coppaelite."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melilitolite - A type of ultramafic-melilitic-rock. Melilitolite is the general name for coarse-grained melilitic rocks, and they are classified according to their melilite - olivine - clinopyroxene content. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 6.2 and fig. 28a."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MELR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Melilitic rock - A type of exotic crystalline igneous rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is defined as a rock that contains more than 10% modal melilite. Although light-coloured, melilite is classified as a mafic mineral belonging to group M. Melilitic rocks are divided into ultramafic-melilitic-rock, and non-ultramafic-melilitic-rock. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 6.2 and figs. 27, 28."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MES> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Medium-sand [Unlithified Deposits Coding Scheme - Extended]"@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MESO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Metasomatic-rock - A heterogeneous group of metamorphic rocks where metamorphism has involved a significant change in the chemistry of the protolith. Rocks commonly classified as metasomatic include fenite, greisen, rodingites, and skarn. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/02, section 8."@en .
<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/METR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Metamorphic rock [Obsolete code: use +#MET]"@en .
